  "prefLabel": "Man 208.08 Prehearing Conference",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Man 208.08 Prehearing Conference. Any party may request, or the presiding officer shall schedule on his or her own initiative, a prehearing conference in accordance with RSA 541-A:31, V to consider:\n\n(a) Offers of settlement;\n\n(b) Simplification of the issues;\n\n(c) Stipulations or admissions as to issues of fact or proof by consent of the parties;\n\n(d) Limitations on the number of witnesses;\n\n(e) Changes to standard procedures desired during the hearing by consent of the parties;\n\n(f) Consolidation of examination of witnesses; or\n\n(g) Any other matters which aid in the disposition of the proceeding.\n\nSource. #8286-A, eff 2-16-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/man100-400.html"
